<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Brassica oleracea Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 172 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Brassica oleracea)",
        "Brassica oleracea Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 172 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Brassica oleracea morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Brassica oleracea specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Brassica oleracea" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg u and v are identified Brassica morphogens",
        "does_not_claim: That the nonlinear sweep Pearson r exceeds 0.98 (it is 0.8266)",
        "does_not_claim: That this wavelength model replaces the Azpeitia plastochron account",
        "reconstructed_in_script: D_v = 51.752 so the fastest mode is 172 µm (13 px, 24 waves, 4128 µm patch)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian at a=0.10, b=0.90 and sigma(k) on a periodic grid",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Modal growth fit, D_v sweep with separate RMSE, equal-diffusion ablation, excess-green curd metrics",
        "reported_in_source: Azpeitia et al. 2021 DOI 10.1126/science.abg5999: Romanesco cones from a reiterated floral network",
        "reported_in_source: Duclos and Björkman 2008: the curd is proliferating inflorescence meristem",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v + Du lap u and dv/dt = b - u^2 v + Dv lap v",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: linear dispersion selects a wavenumber k_c",
        "transfer_boundary: 15 µm is the successor cell-scale boundary used to test stability, not a new measured epidermal diameter",
        "transfer_boundary: 172 µm is the MorphoEval detail length for slot 3137, not a figure in Azpeitia or Duclos",
        "transfer_boundary: The animated field is a primordium-scale spot texture. The photograph is a macro curd. Fitness is statistical, not a registered overlay" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/brassica_oleracea_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Brassica oleracea; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: linear dispersion selects a wavenumber k_c | Schnakenberg 1979: du/dt = a - u + u^2 v + Du lap u and dv/dt = b - u^2 v + Dv lap v | Azpeitia et al. 2021 DOI 10.1126/science.abg5999: Romanesco cones from a reiterated floral network | Duclos and Björkman 2008: the curd is proliferating inflorescence meristem; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian at a=0.10, b=0.90 and sigma(k) on a periodic grid | D_v = 51.752 so the fastest mode is 172 µm (13 px, 24 waves, 4128 µm patch) | Modal growth fit, D_v sweep with separate RMSE, equal-diffusion ablation, excess-green curd metrics; transfer_boundary: 172 µm is the MorphoEval detail length for slot 3137, not a figure in Azpeitia or Duclos | The animated field is a primordium-scale spot texture. The photograph is a macro curd. Fitness is statistical, not a registered overlay | 15 µm is the successor cell-scale boundary used to test stability, not a new measured epidermal diameter; does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg u and v are identified Brassica morphogens | That this wavelength model replaces the Azpeitia plastochron account | That the nonlinear sweep Pearson r exceeds 0.98 (it is 0.8266)]; phenomenon_size: 7.6 cm (0.07562 m, log10=-1.121 m, tier=7_organism_cm); species_scale_ladder (1 runs from 7.6 cm to 7.6 cm): 7.6 cm:roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00289234>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/jxb/erm327>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1179047>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5999> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-27-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-audit-v2-delphi10000-brassica-oleracea-turing-wavelength-s0-8> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion & Turing Dispersion" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.88e-01 .

